    "title": "Winston-Salem police search for suspect after chase, wrong-way crash in area of U.S. 421, 5th Street - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Dolan Reynolds ,\n4 hours ago\nWINSTON-SALEM, N.C. (WGHP) — Winston-Salem police are searching for a suspect after a chase and crash on Wednesday night.\nAt 8:38 p.m., officers were trying to stop a male driver with outstanding warrants, according to the Winston-Salem Police Department.\nThey tried blocking him in at 14 th Street and Liberty Street when police say the man rammed into an unmarked police car with its lights on.\nA chase then began. FOX8 is told the chase took place in the city and the county.\nThe driver got off U.S. 421 at 1 st Street. The driver then continued into downtown Winston-Salem, so the WSPD called off the chase for safety reasons.\nPolice say the driver hit an uninvolved civilian’s vehicle in the area of 1 st Street. The person’s vehicle was damaged, but the person was not hurt.\nUnmarked officers then found the driver again. At one point, the driver almost ran into another officer.\nThe driver continued on U.S. 421 while going the wrong way and wrecked in the area of 5 th Street and U.S. 421.\nOfficers found a female with the driver, who ran away.\nThey are still searching for the driver.\nNo officers were injured.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX8 WGHP.",
